-R . UmbraCrypto
-R ../update-core/proofs-coq Lib
-R ../chain-core/proofs-coq Lib

# umbra-update-core — the CRYPTOGRAPHIC layer (issue #58).
#
# Kept in its own directory, with its own _CoqProject, for one reason: the
# game-based part depends on SSProve, which drags in mathcomp + mathcomp-analysis
# + extructures + deriving + equations. The 12-file update-core chain next door
# must stay buildable with a bare Coq 8.18 and NOTHING else, so it can never be
# allowed to acquire that dependency. Everything here `Require`s across the
# directory boundary; nothing next door requires anything here.
#
# TIERS.
#   Tier D (deterministic, bare Coq)  — Update_Forgery.v, Update_Encoding.v,
#     Umbra_DeviceLink.v.
#     No mathcomp. Buildable with `./build.sh --det-only`. These are the files
#     that consume the `Qed`s next door and hand the crypto layer a purely
#     syntactic interface.
#   Tier G (game-based, needs SSProve) — Umbra_EUFCMA.v, Umbra_Reduction.v.
#
# See README.md for the install recipe, the assumption budget and the list of
# what is NOT proved.

# --- Tier D: deterministic. Bare Coq 8.18, no mathcomp. ------------------
# The reduction core: acceptance yields a valid, fresh (message, tag) pair.
Update_Forgery.v
# The Aeneas <-> plain-Z type bridge, and the theorem that makes the reduction
# implementable by a key-less party: on acceptance the encoding of the DEVICE'S
# preimage/tag equals the encoding computed from the WIRE bytes alone.
Update_Encoding.v
# The CANONICAL preimage decoding: base-257 digits back to the 75 byte values,
# so the abstract MAC can be DEFINED as the seam applied to that decoding
# instead of chosen classically. Also states, as a theorem, which package bytes
# the tag does and does not cover.
Umbra_Canonical.v
# The BYTE-VALID SUBIMAGE: re-indexes the message space at `256^60`, the exact
# set of 60-byte authenticated cores, so every game message decodes to seventy-
# five genuine bytes and the base-257 dead zone is unreachable.
Umbra_ByteSpace.v
# The AUDIT of the one premise that re-indexing leaves: `ArrayVectors` is
# SATISFIABLE in the same list model that witnesses
# `Update_Model.quarantine_has_a_model` — so it cannot have made the axiom set
# inconsistent, nor displaced any of the twenty laws — and it is NECESSARY:
# deny it at one message and the dead-zone counterexample rebuilds there.
# Exactly the right premise, with no slack in either direction.
Umbra_ArrayVectors.v
# The joint: real acceptance implies the game's win condition. Takes the game's
# MAC over an ARBITRARY key type so it stays out of the mathcomp tier.
Umbra_DeviceLink.v
# The wire: a package space that IS a choice_type (`list nat`), the device's
# marshalling into `slice u8`, and the REAL acceptance predicate as a `bool`.
# This is what lets the extracted parser appear inside an SSProve oracle.
Umbra_Wire.v
# The CONVERSE parser: acceptance implies the five key-free guards, and those
# guards drive the extracted body all the way to the tag comparison. This is
# what turns Umbra_RealGame's `Hfactorise` from a hypothesis into a theorem.
Update_Converse.v
# The same factorisation at the wire, plus the CONCRETE key-free `struct_ok`
# the SSProve reduction evaluates.
Umbra_WireConverse.v
# THE UNION, deterministic half. Two packages the parser accepts whose 60-byte
# AUTHENTICATED CORES agree have equal blob bodies, or the chained seam
# collided. No tag hypothesis and no package-MAC collision disjunct, unlike
# `Chain_Compose`. This is the first file here to require `chain-core` (third
# `-R` above); chain-core must therefore be BUILT FIRST, and `build.sh` guards
# on it. The edge runs one way: nothing in chain-core requires anything here.
Umbra_UnionCore.v

# --- Tier G: game-based. Needs SSProve (see README.md). ------------------
Umbra_EUFCMA.v
Umbra_Reduction.v
# The reduction with the extracted parser IN the `submit` oracle. Unlike
# Umbra_Reduction.v, this file does not compile if `parse_and_verify` is
# removed, and its `Print Assumptions` lists the Aeneas axioms.
Umbra_RealGame.v
# THE UNION, game half: the case split on the game's own query set. Joins the
# tag-reuse tier to the fresh-tag tier, and states -- as a negative -- the two
# obstructions that stop the three disjuncts becoming one probability bound.
Umbra_Union.v
